<h2>FAQ Section</h2>
<h3>What are the most important home service marketing statistics for 2025?</h3>
<p>The most critical statistics are: 97% of consumers read reviews before choosing a contractor (BrightLocal, 2026), 78% of customers hire the first contractor to respond (HomeAdvisor, 2025), and 46% of all Google searches have local intent (Google, 2025). These three stats alone prove that reviews, speed, and local SEO are the foundation of home service marketing.</p>
<h3>How much should a home service business spend on marketing?</h3>
<p>The standard recommendation is 7–12% of gross revenue, with startups spending 12–20% and established brands spending 5–8%. The most successful home service businesses allocate 65–70% of their marketing budget to digital channels, with 40% going to paid ads, 35% to SEO and content, and 25% to customer retention (industry benchmarks, 2025).</p>
<h3>What is a good cost per lead for home services?</h3>
<p>The average cost per lead for home improvement businesses is $90.92 (WordStream, 2025). However, this varies significantly by trade: HVAC averages $92, plumbing $52, electrical $58, and roofing $228. Referral leads cost $0–$25 and close at 50%+ rates, making them the most efficient channel.</p>
<h3>How important are Google reviews for contractors?</h3>
<p>Extremely important. 97% of consumers read reviews for local businesses, 68% will not use a business under 4 stars, and a 1-star improvement can increase revenue by 5–9%. Reviews also contribute approximately 17% to local pack rankings, making them critical for both trust and visibility.</p>
<h3>What is the ideal response time for home service leads?</h3>
<p>Under 5 minutes is the target. Responding within 60 seconds achieves a 47% conversion rate, while a 30-minute response drops to 16%. 78% of customers hire the first contractor to respond, so speed is often more important than price or reputation.</p>
<h3>How fast should a contractor website load?</h3>
<p>Under 3 seconds is the minimum standard, with under 2 seconds being ideal. 53% of mobile users abandon sites that take longer than 3 seconds to load, and a 1-second delay reduces conversions by up to 20%. Use Google PageSpeed Insights to audit your site.</p>
<h3>Is AI search really a threat to traditional local SEO?</h3>
<p>AI search is a shift, not a threat. 45% of consumers now use AI tools for local recommendations (up from 6% in 2025), and AI search visitors convert at 4.4x higher rates. The businesses that optimize for AI search (complete GBP, structured data, consistent citations) will capture the highest-converting traffic.</p>
<h3>What percentage of home service leads come from mobile?</h3>
<p>65% of all website traffic and 70% of local searches come from mobile devices. 78% of local mobile searches result in an offline purchase, making mobile optimization the highest-ROI investment for most contractors.</p>
<h3>How many reviews does a contractor need?</h3>
<p>The minimum threshold is 7 reviews (the average number homeowners read before feeling confident), but the competitive standard is 50+ reviews with a 4.5+ star rating. Top-ranked businesses in the Local Pack average approximately 240 Google reviews.</p>
<h3>Should home service businesses use Google Local Services Ads?</h3>
<p>Yes. LSAs typically deliver leads at $15–$50 — lower than traditional Google Ads. They also include the Google Guaranteed badge, use pay-per-lead pricing, and capture 13.8% of SERP clicks. For most contractors, LSAs should be the first paid channel to test.</p>
